                "Good morning! Today I will tell you about my typical <span class='mark'>school</span> day. <img src='https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1523050854058-8df90110c9f1' alt='School building' width='300'> My name is Tom, and I am twelve years old. I study at Greenfield Middle School. It's a nice school with friendly teachers and students.",
                "My day starts early. The <span class='mark'>alarm clock</span> rings at 6:30 AM. I wake up and stretch. First, I go to the <span class='mark'>bathroom</span> to wash my face and brush my teeth. Then I get dressed in my school uniform. Our uniform is blue and white - a blue shirt, gray trousers, and black shoes.",
                "At 7:00 AM, I go downstairs for <span class='mark'>breakfast</span>. My mother prepares breakfast every morning. Today we have scrambled eggs, toast, and orange juice. I eat quickly because I don't want to be late for school. After breakfast, I brush my teeth again and pack my school bag.",
                "My school starts at 8:00 AM, but I need to leave home at 7:30 AM. I walk to school with my friend <span class='mark'>James</span>. James lives next door. We meet at 7:30 exactly. The walk to school takes about fifteen minutes. We talk about homework, games, and our plans for the weekend.",
                "When we arrive at school, we go directly to our <span class='mark'>classroom</span>. Our classroom is on the second floor, room 205. It's a bright room with big windows. There are twenty desks arranged in rows. Each desk has two chairs. I sit next to my friend Lisa.",
                "The first lesson starts at 8:00 AM sharp. Today, Monday, we have <span class='mark'>mathematics</span> first. Our math teacher is Mr. Johnson. He is tall and kind. He explains new concepts clearly. Today we learn about fractions. At first, it seems difficult, but Mr. Johnson gives us many examples.",
                "Mathematics lasts for 45 minutes. At 8:45 AM, we have a short <span class='mark'>break</span>. During the break, we go to the playground. Some students eat snacks. Others play games. I usually talk with my friends or drink water from the fountain.",
                "The second lesson is <span class='mark'>English</span>. Our English teacher is Mrs. Wilson. She speaks very clearly. Today we read a short story about a boy and his dog. After reading, we answer questions about the story. Then we learn new vocabulary words. Mrs. Wilson writes the words on the whiteboard.",
                "After English, we have <span class='mark'>science</span>. Science is my favorite subject. Today we learn about plants. Our teacher, Ms. Garcia, shows us pictures of different plants. She explains how plants make their own food through photosynthesis. We also look at real leaves under a microscope.",
                "At 10:30 AM, we have a longer break - 20 minutes. This is our <span class='mark'>snack time</span>. I eat the sandwich my mother prepared. It's ham and cheese today. I also have an apple. Some students buy food from the school canteen. The canteen sells sandwiches, fruit, and drinks.",
                "After the break, we have <span class='mark'>history</span>. History is interesting but sometimes difficult because there are many dates to remember. Today we learn about ancient Egypt. We see pictures of pyramids and pharaohs. Our teacher tells us about the Nile River and how important it was for Egyptian civilization.",
                "The last lesson before lunch is <span class='mark'>art</span>. I enjoy art class because we can be creative. Today we paint with watercolors. The teacher gives us the theme 'My Dream House'. I paint a house with a big garden and a swimming pool. My friend James paints a treehouse.",
                "Lunchtime is at 12:30 PM. We have one hour for lunch. Most students eat in the school <span class='mark'>cafeteria</span>. <img src='https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1564759298141-cef86f51d4d4' alt='School cafeteria' width='300'> The cafeteria serves different meals every day. Today there's chicken with rice, vegetable soup, or pasta. I choose chicken with rice. I sit with my friends Lisa, James, and Sam.",
                "After lunch, we have <span class='mark'>physical education</span> (PE). We change into our sports clothes in the locker room. Today we play football in the school field. I'm not very good at football, but I try my best. Running and playing with friends is fun. PE class makes me feel energetic.",
                "The final lesson of the day is <span class='mark'>music</span>. In music class, we learn to play the recorder. Today we practice a simple song called 'Happy Melody'. Our music teacher, Mr. Lee, is very patient. He shows us how to place our fingers correctly. By the end of the lesson, most of us can play the song.",
                "School finishes at 3:00 PM. Our teacher gives us <span class='mark'>homework</span> for tomorrow. We have math exercises and English vocabulary to learn. I write the homework in my notebook carefully so I don't forget.",
